Z||000003||ChadMan||01-15-2000||10:47 AM||||Mid-Ohio is about 50 miles north-northeast of Columbus, just outside of Mansfield, OH.  From Pittsburgh, I'd guess it would be around 2 hrs.<P>I used to work as a PR intern for Mid-Ohio, so I could handle all the registration business.  Last year, five of us from COFE went up, but everything was FUBAR and I was the only one who pre-registered (and was therefore the only one who got to drive around the track).<P>There are a couple of good places where we could rendezvous to drive on up to the track - the one that seems to make the most sense would be the McDonald's or Wendy's at the junction of I-71 and SR 95.  From there it's only about 15 minutes to the track.||||reg||1
