Z||000013||ChadMan||01-17-2000||10:18 AM||||This response is great, you guys.  I won't be the only Fiero out there this year!<P>For now, we really don't need to do anything because the event is so far away.  Around early-to-mid May, I'll dig up this thread and call for names of all you guys and girls who want to participate.  Then I'll call Steve Bidlack at Mid-Ohio and get a pre-reg form and send it in with everybody's names.  We can then discuss where to meet on the morning of the event!<P>The only cost to participate is admission to the track.  Once we're at the track and parked in the Fiero Club corral, we all need to sign an "If I kill myself it's my own damn fault" waiver.  Then, during the lunch break, we'll get to take a couple of parade laps with all the other car clubs.  After lunch, each club selects its best car to participate in the Concours d'Elegance.  It's doubtful we'll win anything (past winners have included an immaculate MG TD and a 62 Corvette) but what the hey!||||reg||1
