Z||000025||Eric||02-14-2000||02:29 PM||||For someone who has done this before (Chadman?), what can we expect to go on at this event?  Are there many cars lined up on display like a car show or is mainly just a way to turn a couple laps on the track?  If it's not the later, can I suggest a Fiero racing event?  Other car clubs do it all the time, but unless you do it in conjunction with many Fiero clubs, it would be expensive to pay for the track times.  I don't know how these things work and, Chadman, you would be the perfect man to ask since you said you used to work for the track.||||reg||1
Z||000026||ChadMan||02-14-2000||04:12 PM||||Good question, Eric.  The Mid-Ohio meet is strictly a show.  The main appeal as I see it will be to hang out with other Fieroholics, see a lot of really nice cars (Fiero and otherwise - there are lots of Vettes, Porsches, Brit cars, etc) and take a few parade laps.  The only way we'll get over 50 mph is if the Vette guys start racing one another like they did last year.<P>Now if you actually want to drive your Fiero at speed on a race track, I think the best deal going is Nelson Ledges "Fundayz."  For $300, they offer a three-day program: one day of classroom instruction and two days of on-track fast lapping including lots of solo time.  The classroom day is mandatory, but once you've completed the program, you can come back later and spend a day on track for $100.<P>By comparison, the Mid-Ohio School wants $550 for their one-day high-performance driving program, and only half the day is spent on track.<P>I think the Nelson Ledges thing could be a lot of fun.  It's not cheap, but I can't think of a cheaper way to spend two days on a real racetrack at speed.  And the class counts toward getting your SCCA racing license.  What do you guys think?<P>Info on Nelson Ledges Fundayz can be found at <A HREF="http://fastone.com/Nelson99/dayz9.html." TARGET=_blank>http://fastone.com/Nelson99/dayz9.html.</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||ChadMan||02-14-2000||04:16 PM||||Dammit, the period in that URL is playing tricks with IE's mind.  Try this:<BR> <A HREF="http://fastone.com/Nelson99/dayz9.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fastone.com/Nelson99/dayz9.html</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000028||Eric||02-14-2000||07:27 PM||||Sounds good to me.  I'm a little confused about not being able to sign up ahead of time.  It would seem to me, that it would be really difficult to get into, if it's first come first serve.  Have you ever done this, Chadman?  Maybe we could organize a group to assure ourselves a position.  Anybody else interested?  Seems like you can really get your money's worth from a program like this.||||reg||14
Z||000029||ChadMan||02-15-2000||09:11 AM||||I've never been to Nelson Ledges, but I did get to take the one-day HP class at Mid-Ohio for free at the close of the 1993 season.  Here's the World War I flying ace in his Sopwith Camel:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84coupe.jpg"> <BR>Look at those poor 80-series Michelins curling under!<P>It looks like if you get a group together, you can pre-register, so maybe that would be our best bet.  If you click on their calendar, there's a three-day session in early June that looks promising and another in late July.||||reg||1
