Z||000034||2M4 Dale||05-23-2000||12:14 PM||||OK guys, we're about a month away now and I thought I'd drag this old string back up.<P>Hey Chadman, how soon before advance tickets go on sale for the Vintage Gran Prix. (I want the cheap/discounted tickets...lol)<P>And, how do we go about pre-registering?<p>[This message has been edited by 2M4 Dale (edited 05-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000035||ChadMan||05-23-2000||02:44 PM||||Thanks for getting me in gear, Dale.  I just sent an email to a couple of guys from Cleveland Fieros to see if they have registered for a corral.  I will also call Central Ohio Fiero Enthusiasts' president tonight to check with him, so I should know something by tomorrow morning.<P>If either group has already registered, participation will be as simple as emailing our names to Cleveland Fieros or COFE, buying general-admission tickets, and parking in the Fiero Club corral on Sunday, 7/25.<P>If neither group has registered, I can call Mid-Ohio's director of PR and get us a corral.  But I will only do this if we have at least six or seven people who will definitely show up with their Fieros on 7/25.<P>Tickets are $22 at the gate, but you can get a 10% discount by ordering tickets before June 16th.  I will post here as soon as I know what the deal is.||||reg||1
